<title>UK: ICO coffee exports up at 7.40 mln bags in March.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports up at 7.40 mln bags in March.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Coffee Organization (ICO) said on Tuesday exporting members' exports fell slightly to 7.40 million 60-kg bags in March from 7.41 million in February but up sharply from 6.47 million in March 1996.</p>
<p>In the 12 months to March 1997, total exports rose to 79.88 million bags from 69.71 million in the same 1996 period.</p>
<p>In the first six months of the current 1996/97 coffee year to March total exports were up at 42.63 million bags from 36.78 million in the same 1995/96 period.  </p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included --</p>
<p>		   March 97   March 96  Oct/March 96/97 Oct/March 95/96</p>
<p>    Brazil	 1,631	 761	10,185	    5,613</p>
<p>    Colombia	 727	 909	 5,955	    5,854</p>
<p>    Guatemala	577	 523	 2,711	    2,040</p>
<p>    Mexico	   676	 633	 3,260	    2,943</p>
<p>    Indonesia	186	 248	 2,064	    2,136</p>
<p>    Uganda	   336	 438	 2,675	    2,363</p>
<p>    Vietnam	  772	 335	 3,789	    2,572</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast    339	 365	 1,045	    1,087</p>
<p>-- Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
</text>
